THOUGHT: The previous sed command incorrectly duplicated @Override annotations, causing compilation errors. I need to clean up the method signatures manually: keep a single @Override on each method, add @Nullable on the return types, and mark the defaultValue parameter as @Nullable. Then I’ll re-run the build to ensure the NullAway error count decreases and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '212,231c\  @Nullable
  @Override
  public <T extends Enum<T>> T getEnumValue(String propertyName, Class<T> enumType) {
    return this.getEnumValue(propertyName, enumType, null);
  }

  @Nullable
  @Override
  public <T extends Enum<T>> T getEnumValue(
      String propertyName, Class<T> enumType, @Nullable T defaultValue) {
    ICustomProperty property = this.getProperty(propertyName);
    if (property == null) {
      return defaultValue;
    }

    T value = property.getAsEnum(enumType);
    if (value == null) {
      return defaultValue;
    }

    return value;
  }
